---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION, EDITOR_NAME, EDITOR_URL } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
  title={"About — " + SITE_TITLE}
  description="How terminalblog covers AI coding agents: human editorial oversight, observable sources, and transparent AI-assisted research."
>
  <article class="content">
    <h1 style="font-size:1.75rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">About {SITE_TITLE}</h1>

    <p>
      <strong>{SITE_TITLE}</strong> tracks the rapidly evolving ecosystem of coding agents
      — autonomous AI assistants that go beyond simple chat completions to plan, execute, and deliver
      complex software engineering tasks.
    </p>

    <h2>Editor</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_TITLE} is edited by
      <a href={EDITOR_URL}><strong>{EDITOR_NAME}</strong></a>.
      Research and first drafts are assisted by AI agent personas (see
      <a href="/writers/">writers</a>), but every article is reviewed against primary sources —
      GitHub issues, commits, release notes, and public discussions — before it stays on the site.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--fg-dim);">
      Corrections welcome: open an issue on
      <a href="https://github.com/Anshad2u/terminalblog">GitHub</a>
      or mention us on
      <a href="https://x.com/terminalblog_en">X</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What We Track</h2>

    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0.75rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      <div style="padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;">
        <strong>Hermes Agent</strong>
        <p style="font-size:0.85rem;margin:0.25rem 0 0;">The most full-featured open-source agent. Background tasks, MOA, cron, memory, skills.</p>
        <a href="/tool/hermes/" style="font-size:0.8rem;">View articles →</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;">
        <strong>Claude Code</strong>
        <p style="font-size:0.85rem;margin:0.25rem 0 0;">Anthropic's terminal coding agent with enterprise Gateway and plugin system.</p>
        <a href="/tool/claude-code/" style="font-size:0.8rem;">View articles →</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;">
        <strong>OpenCode</strong>
        <p style="font-size:0.85rem;margin:0.25rem 0 0;">Skill-driven coding agent with slash command workflows and SKILL.md execution model.</p>
        <a href="/tool/opencode/" style="font-size:0.8rem;">View articles →</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;">
        <strong>Mimo Code</strong>
        <p style="font-size:0.85rem;margin:0.25rem 0 0;">OpenCode fork with vision support and reasoning model integration.</p>
        <a href="/tool/mimo/" style="font-size:0.8rem;">View articles →</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;">
        <strong>Kilo Code CLI</strong>
        <p style="font-size:0.85rem;margin:0.25rem 0 0;">Lightweight LLM orchestrator for quick AI-assisted tasks.</p>
        <a href="/tool/kilo/" style="font-size:0.8rem;">View articles →</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;">
        <strong>pi.dev</strong>
        <p style="font-size:0.85rem;margin:0.25rem 0 0;">Personal intelligence agents with persistent knowledge graphs.</p>
        <a href="/tool/pi-dot-dev/" style="font-size:0.8rem;">View articles →</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;">
        <strong>Oh My Pi</strong>
        <p style="font-size:0.85rem;margin:0.25rem 0 0;">Hash-anchored coding agent with LSP, browser, subagents, and IDE-level tools.</p>
        <a href="/tool/oh-my-pi/" style="font-size:0.8rem;">View articles →</a>
      </div>
      <div style="padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;">
        <strong>Gitlawb Zero</strong>
        <p style="font-size:0.85rem;margin:0.25rem 0 0;">Decentralized terminal agent you fully own.</p>
        <a href="/tool/gitlawb-zero/" style="font-size:0.8rem;">View articles →</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="font-size:0.9rem;">
      Full adoption rankings live on the
      <a href="/leaderboard/">leaderboard</a>.
      All tracked agents are listed on the homepage table.
    </p>

    <h2>Methodology</h2>
    <p>
      We prioritize <strong>observable signal</strong> over rumor: GitHub issues, release commits,
      npm/download stats, security reports, and developer discussions. Deep-dives (especially
      security “Beware” posts) stay valuable past a single release cycle. Ephemeral commit roundups
      are secondary to durable guides, comparisons, and security analysis.
    </p>
    <ul style="font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.6;">
      <li>One story, one URL — near-duplicates are redirected to a canonical post.</li>
      <li>Tool hubs only for real coding agents (not generic news tags).</li>
      <li>Affiliate or partner links are disclosed when present.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Disclosure</h2>
    <p style="font-size:0.9rem;">
      Some articles may include affiliate links (for example product or plan comparisons).
      Editorial coverage is not sold. If we earn a commission, it does not change rankings or security findings.
    </p>

    <h2>Open Source</h2>
    <p>
      This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, deployed on
      <a href="https://vercel.com">Vercel</a>.
      Source: <a href="https://github.com/Anshad2u/terminalblog">github.com/Anshad2u/terminalblog</a>.
      CLI: <code>npx terminalblog</code> —
      <a href="https://github.com/Anshad2u/terminalblog-cli">terminalblog-cli</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
